      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to question this bias; relying on \"aggressive\" vocabulary often unintentionally penalizes speakers of specific dialects while allowing coded hate speech to pass under the radar. A responsible moderation system must flag Post 4 and similar \"clean\" statements as potential hate speech or harassment because they targets protected groups or incites harm, regardless of the tone or slang used. To avoid this, the filter should be calibrated to detect the *target* of the speech and the *intent* to harm, rather than just measuring the raw emotional intensity of the words. Correctly identifying the intent behind seemingly calm discussions about demographics is crucial for building a truly safe platform.",
